    "summary_one_sentence": "Gravely wounded after a brutal final battle, an aging Robin Hood reflects on a life marked by violence and crime while seeking redemption in the care of a mysterious woman.",
    "summary_short": "After surviving a ferocious battle he believed would be his last, an aging Robin Hood is left severely injured and forced to confront the dark legacy of his violent past. He is rescued by a mysterious woman who tends to his wounds and offers him an unexpected path toward spiritual salvation. As he grapples with the weight of his crimes, Robin must decide if he is truly worthy of forgiveness. This gritty reimagining explores the final days of the legendary outlaw as he faces his greatest internal struggle.",
    "summary_long": "The legendary outlaw Robin Hood finds himself at the end of his journey, physically broken and spiritually haunted by a lifetime of warfare, crime, and bloodshed. Following a devastating clash that he assumed would claim his life, he crawls away from the battlefield with mortal wounds. Instead of meeting a lonely end, he is discovered and taken in by a mysterious woman possessing deep wisdom and hidden motives. As she nurses him back to health in a secluded sanctuary, Robin is forced to look back at the trail of violence he left behind in the name of justice. The woman challenges his perceptions of his own legacy, forcing him to confront the grim reality of the lives he has taken. Throughout his recovery, external threats still loom, but Robin's primary battle becomes an internal quest for peace and absolution. He struggles with the guilt of his past misdeeds, wondering if the good he accomplished can ever outweigh the blood on his hands. Ultimately, the film strips away the romanticized myth of the heroic archer to deliver a somber character study about mortality. In his final hours, Robin Hood must choose between succumbing to his past demons or embracing the hard-fought salvation offered to him.",
    "synopsis": "This gripping and introspective drama offers a gritty, revisionist look at the twilight days of folklore's most famous outlaw. Grappling with the heavy psychological toll of a life defined by crime, murder, and warfare, an aging Robin Hood finds himself gravely injured after a brutal battle he fully expected to be his last. Left at death's door, his fate takes an unexpected turn when he falls into the hands of a mysterious woman. Sheltered from the outside world, he is offered a profound chance at salvation and closure, forcing the legendary hero to confront his darkest regrets and decide what his legacy will truly be before time runs out.",
